WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.779
Two laws run India's elections.

2
00:00:02.779 --> 00:00:04.164
Passed a year apart,

3
00:00:04.164 --> 00:00:06.151
they do different jobs.

4
00:00:06.476 --> 00:00:08.161
The 1950 Act deals with

5
00:00:08.161 --> 00:00:10.387
seats and electoral rolls: who

6
00:00:10.387 --> 00:00:11.999
votes, and where.

7
00:00:11.999 --> 00:00:13.879
The 1951 Act covers how

8
00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.439
elections are run,

9
00:00:15.439 --> 00:00:16.716
who can stand,

10
00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.923
and corrupt practices.

11
00:00:19.283 --> 00:00:21.135
Under Section 8 of the

12
00:00:21.135 --> 00:00:22.043
1951 Act,

13
00:00:22.043 --> 00:00:24.114
a conviction with 2 years

14
00:00:24.114 --> 00:00:26.547
or more in prison disqualifies

15
00:00:26.547 --> 00:00:27.759
a lawmaker.

16
00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:29.010
For the jail term,

17
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.268
and six years after release.

18
00:00:31.606 --> 00:00:33.512
Sitting members once had three

19
00:00:33.512 --> 00:00:35.418
months to appeal before losing

20
00:00:35.418 --> 00:00:36.441
their seat.

21
00:00:36.441 --> 00:00:37.699
In Lily Thomas,

22
00:00:37.699 --> 00:00:40.018
2013, the Supreme Court struck

23
00:00:40.018 --> 00:00:42.080
that protection down.

24
00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.635
Your turn.

25
00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:46.444
Which Act covers electoral rolls?
